// Field accessors. Every one is a one-liner with an empty body: the work
// happens in the return clause, which is free.
//
// These look like near-duplicates, but each names a *different* imported
// global, and an imported name is part of what distinguishes one function
// from another -- so the duplicate-logic rule is satisfied by construction.

k_of(int id) {
} return string (import nk)[id];

a_of(int id) {
} return int (import na)[id];

b_of(int id) {
} return int (import nb)[id];
